+# Paper-Window Real-Data Workflow
+
+The `Paper Window Real Data Replication` workflow is a manual-only workflow for running the closest available public-data reconstruction of the AGENTICAITA paper window.
+
+Defaults:
+
+- window: `2026-04-06T00:00:00Z` through `2026-04-11T23:59:59Z`;
+- timeframe: `1m`;
+- profile: `baseline-15`;
+- baseline symbol count: `15`.
+
+Modes:
+
+| Mode | Behaviour |
+| --- | --- |
+| `closest` | Attempts Hyperliquid first, then falls back to Binance USD-M if Hyperliquid does not produce complete exportable OHLCV coverage. |
+| `hyperliquid` | Attempts only Hyperliquid. |
+| `binanceusdm` | Uses Binance USD-M perpetual futures as a public comparable-market fallback. |
+
+The workflow runs `scripts/run_real_data_replication.py`, `scripts/check_replication_quality.py`, run-manifest generation, local result indexing, dashboard rendering, a GitHub Actions summary, and a compact artefact upload.
+
+It does not upload raw SQLite databases or raw per-symbol OHLCV CSV directories by default. Set `upload_replication_input` to `true` only when the exported replication CSV is needed for review.
+
+This is not an exact reproduction of the paper run. Public APIs can reconstruct comparable market-condition inputs, but they do not recover the original L2 order book snapshots, prompts, LLM calls, agent deliberations, risk-manager approvals, SQLite dry-run records, or execution assumptions.
+
